# PART 4 — Create Apex Class

## Step 4

Go to:
Setup → Apex Classes → New

Paste the following code.

```java
public class EmployeeManagementSystem {

    // INSERT EMPLOYEE
    public static void addEmployee(Integer empId, String empName,
                                   String email, Date birthDate,
                                   String dept) {

        Employee__c emp = new Employee__c();

        emp.Emp_ID__c = empId;
        emp.Emp_Name__c = empName;
        emp.Email__c = email;
        emp.Birth_Date__c = birthDate;
        emp.Department__c = dept;

        insert emp;

        System.debug('Employee Added Successfully');
    }


    // VIEW EMPLOYEES
    public static void viewEmployees() {

        List<Employee__c> empList = [
            SELECT Id, Emp_ID__c, Emp_Name__c,
                   Email__c, Birth_Date__c,
                   Department__c
            FROM Employee__c
        ];

        for(Employee__c emp : empList) {
            System.debug(
                'Employee ID: ' + emp.Emp_ID__c +
                ' Name: ' + emp.Emp_Name__c +
                ' Email: ' + emp.Email__c +
                ' Department: ' + emp.Department__c
            );
        }
    }


    // UPDATE EMPLOYEE
    public static void updateEmployee(Integer empId,
                                      String newDept) {

        Employee__c emp = [
            SELECT Id, Department__c
            FROM Employee__c
            WHERE Emp_ID__c = :empId
            LIMIT 1
        ];

        emp.Department__c = newDept;

        update emp;

        System.debug('Employee Updated Successfully');
    }


    // DELETE EMPLOYEE
    public static void deleteEmployee(Integer empId) {

        Employee__c emp = [
            SELECT Id
            FROM Employee__c
            WHERE Emp_ID__c = :empId
            LIMIT 1
        ];

        delete emp;

        System.debug('Employee Deleted Successfully');
    }
}
```

Save the class.

